# {{.Name}}

A Go REST API scaffold with **liveness**, **readiness**, and **Prometheus metrics**.
Jaeger and Prometheus run from one `docker compose up`{{if or .HasPostgres .HasVault}}, along with{{if .HasPostgres}} Postgres{{end}}{{if and .HasPostgres .HasVault}} and{{end}}{{if .HasVault}} Vault{{end}}{{end}}.

Shared libraries come from [`github.com/benthinnick/distlibs`](https://github.com/benthinnick/distlibs).

## Architecture

```
client ──▶ api HTTP (chi, :8080)   /healthz /readyz /metrics
client ──▶ api gRPC (:9090)        application RPCs
{{if .HasPostgres}}             ├──▶ Postgres (:5432)   readiness probe
{{end}}             ├──▶ jaeger (:16686)    traces over OTLP gRPC
             ├──▶ prometheus (:9090) scrapes /metrics{{if .HasVault}}
             └──▶ vault  (:8200)     secrets, read at startup{{end}}
```

## Quick start

```bash
docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml up --build
```

Then:

```bash
curl localhost:8080/healthz
curl localhost:8080/readyz
curl localhost:8080/metrics
```

Open the Jaeger UI at <http://localhost:16686> and pick the `{{.ServiceName}}`
service.

| Service    | URL                     | Notes                            |
| ---------- | ----------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| API        | http://localhost:8080   | `SERVICE_ID={{.ID}}`             |
| API gRPC   | localhost:9091          | compose maps host 9091 → :9090   |
{{if .HasPostgres}}| Postgres   | localhost:5432          | user/pass/db `{{.Name}}`         |
{{end}}| Jaeger     | http://localhost:16686  | trace UI                         |
| Prometheus | http://localhost:9090   | scrapes `api:8080/metrics`       |
{{if .HasVault}}| Vault      | http://localhost:8200   | dev mode, token `dev-root-token` |
{{end}}

## Local Kubernetes

The API Deployment runs **3 replicas**. The same stack can run on kind (recommended
locally), Docker Desktop Kubernetes, or minikube via manifests in
[`deploy/k8s/`](deploy/k8s/).

### kind (recommended)

Requires [kind](https://kind.sigs.k8s.io/) and `kubectl`. One command creates the
cluster (with host port mappings for every NodePort), builds and loads the API
image, and applies the manifests:

```bash
make kind
```

Useful pieces on their own:

```bash
make kind-up       # recreate the kind cluster named {{.Name}}
make kind-load     # docker build + kind load docker-image
make kind-deploy   # kubectl apply numbered manifests + wait for api
make kind-down     # kind delete cluster --name {{.Name}}
```

### Other local clusters

```bash
docker build -t {{.Name}}-api:local -f build/Dockerfile .

kubectl apply -f deploy/k8s/00-namespace.yaml \
  -f deploy/k8s/01-config.yaml \
  -f deploy/k8s/02-deps.yaml \
  -f deploy/k8s/03-jobs.yaml \
  -f deploy/k8s/04-api.yaml \
  -f deploy/k8s/05-logging.yaml
kubectl -n {{.Name}} rollout status deploy/api
```

Services are exposed with fixed NodePorts (kind maps these to the host via
[`deploy/k8s/kind-config.yaml`](deploy/k8s/kind-config.yaml)):

| Service    | URL                    |
| ---------- | ---------------------- |
| API        | http://localhost:30080 |
| API gRPC   | localhost:30091        |
| Jaeger UI  | http://localhost:30686 |
| Prometheus | http://localhost:30090 |
| Grafana    | http://localhost:30300 |
{{if .HasVault}}| Vault      | http://localhost:30200 |
{{end}}

### Searching logs (Grafana + Loki)

Alloy scrapes pod stdout in the `{{.Name}}` namespace into Loki. Grafana is
provisioned with Loki (default) and Prometheus datasources; anonymous Admin
access is enabled for local use.

1. Open <http://localhost:30300> → **Explore** → datasource **Loki**.
2. Example LogQL:

```logql
{app="api"}
{app="api"} | json | status=`500`
{app="api"} | json | trace_id="<paste-from-jaeger-or-response>"
```

Tear down with:

```bash
make kind-down
# or, without kind: kubectl delete -f deploy/k8s/00-namespace.yaml
```

## Endpoints

| Method | Path       | Behaviour                                              |
| ------ | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| GET    | `/healthz` | Liveness. Never touches a dependency.                  |
| GET    | `/readyz`  | Probes listed dependencies{{if or .HasPostgres .HasVault}} ({{if .HasPostgres}}Postgres{{end}}{{if and .HasPostgres .HasVault}}, {{end}}{{if .HasVault}}Vault when enabled{{end}}){{end}}; 503 if any fail. |
| GET    | `/metrics` | Prometheus exposition (request count, latency, sizes). |

## Configuration

Config is assembled from struct defaults, then environment variables{{if .HasVault}}, then Vault when `VAULT_ENABLED=true`{{end}}. See
[.env.example](.env.example). `SERVICE_ID` defaults to `{{.ID}}`.
{{if .HasVault}}
Vault KV v2 path: `${VAULT_KV_MOUNT}/${VAULT_SECRET_PATH}` (default `secret/{{.Name}}/config`).
Keys Vault may overlay: `log_level` and `otel_traces_sampler_arg`.
{{end}}

## Observability

**Tracing.** [`github.com/benthinnick/distlibs/observability`](https://github.com/benthinnick/distlibs)
builds a `TracerProvider` that batches spans to the OTLP gRPC endpoint.
Server spans are renamed to the chi route pattern after routing.

**Logging.** [`github.com/benthinnick/distlibs/observability`](https://github.com/benthinnick/distlibs)
wraps `slog`'s JSON handler so every record written with a request context
picks up `trace_id` and `span_id`.

**Metrics.** [`github.com/benthinnick/distlibs/httpmw`](https://github.com/benthinnick/distlibs) records RED and
size series on a dedicated Prometheus registry and serves them at `/metrics`.
`/healthz`, `/readyz`, and `/metrics` themselves are not counted. Labels are
`method`, `route` (chi pattern), and `status`.

| Metric | Type | Meaning |
| ------ | ---- | ------- |
| `http_requests_total` | counter | request count |
| `http_request_duration_seconds` | histogram | latency |
| `http_request_size_bytes` | histogram | bytes read from the request body |
| `http_response_size_bytes` | histogram | bytes written in the response |

Example PromQL in the Prometheus UI at <http://localhost:9090>:

```promql
sum by (status) (rate(http_requests_total[1m]))
```

## Development

```bash
go test ./... -count=1
go vet ./...
{{if .HasPostgres}}go generate ./internal/providers   # regenerate mockgen provider mocks
{{end}}```

Usecase unit tests live under `tests/usecase/`.

A `Makefile` wraps the common targets (`make test`, `make up`, `make down`,
`make logs`). `make test` passes `-race`, which needs cgo and a 64-bit C
toolchain; on hosts without one, run `make test TESTFLAGS=`.

## Layout

```
cmd/api/                  entrypoint, wiring, graceful shutdown
internal/config/          layered config
internal/entity/          Health, Readiness, ErrorResponse, generated RPC types
{{if .HasPostgres}}internal/ent/schema/      ent table definitions (owned by this service)
{{end}}internal/proto/           buf-generated protobuf + gRPC stubs
internal/server/          HTTP health routes and generated gRPC service
internal/usecase/         readiness probing and generated RPC methods
internal/providers/       dependency adapters
tests/usecase/            usecase unit tests
build/Dockerfile          multi-stage build onto distroless
deploy/                   compose stack
deploy/k8s/               local Kubernetes manifests + kind-config.yaml
```

Shared HTTP, observability{{if or .HasPostgres .HasVault}},{{end}}{{if .HasPostgres}} postgres{{end}}{{if .HasVault}}, and vault{{end}} helpers come from
[`github.com/benthinnick/distlibs`](https://github.com/benthinnick/distlibs).
